lazar (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Representative María Elvira Salazar seeks another term in a Miami-Dade district that leans Republican by about six points, facing former news anchor Eliott Rodriguez. The national environment favors Democrats this year, and the two recent public polls, both from Democratic-leaning firms, show an essentially tied race, one even and one with Salazar up a point. Most race raters still call the contest Lean Republican, with several saying Likely Republican.\n\nSalazar holds a clear financial edge, with about $2.0 million on hand to Rodriguez's $680,000, and she has outspent him despite his strong $723,000 third quarter. House Democratic leader Hakeem Jeffries has campaigned with Rodriguez as immigration and housing dominate the debate. Prediction markets give Rodriguez roughly a one-in-three chance. Incumbency, money, and district lean make Salazar a modest favorite in a genuinely competitive race.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2129, "margin": -4.43}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2851, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2818, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3773, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2766, "margin": -3.2}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.3218, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3331, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3785, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3582, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3814, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3691, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.3705, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.3683, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.315, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.3051, "margin": -2.8}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.3209, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.3463, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.324, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026